# One-off deploy/repair scripts written against the live server. They are kept
# out of the repo root because that root IS the document root on cPanel: a copy
# of seed_remote.php sitting there was reachable at
# https://muhindomubaraka.com/seed_remote.php and re-ran a database seeder for
# anyone who asked. remote_env.txt holds production secrets. Neither belongs in
# anything that gets pushed or scp'd.
_deploy-oneoffs/

# Build plans, agent briefs and build logs. They describe how the codebase was
# produced rather than what it does, they are no use to anyone reading the repo,
# and a document root is the wrong place for them. Kept alongside the project in
# ../muhindo-app-notes/; the committed history still has every earlier version.
